rogant; relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: reliability 100% (strong). Decision quality quick correct decisions (good). Crew cooperation positive atmosphere (good). Communication difficulty (weak). Egocentric (maybe weak cooperation). Not willing to further education (weak adaptability). Overall strong reliability but communication issues.\n\nB: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (good), good at weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but grumpy and uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). So strengths but cooperation concerns.\n\nC: anticipates dangerous situations (stress resilience, decision), sees complex connections (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership (crew cooperation), but not good at taking criticism (adaptability), unorganized (attention). Mixed.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), concentration (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but arrogant (crew cooperation), weak leadership (crew). So some strengths, but cooperation concerns.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Candidate A has reliability and decision, but communication issues may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress and technical, but uncooperative. Candidate C has anticipation and technical, but unorganized and poor criticism. Candidate D has problem solving and responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich candidate has most balanced strengths with fewer serious concerns? A's communication difficulty could affect safety. B's uncooperative could be serious. C's unorganized could affect attention. D's arrogance could affect crew.\n\nMaybe Candidate A's reliability and positive atmosphere outweigh communication difficulty? But difficulty communicating ideas is a big safety issue. However positive atmosphere suggests good crew environment despite difficulty? Might be contradictory.\n\nCandidate B's stress handling and technical are strong, but uncooperative is concerning.\n\nCandidate C's anticipation and leadership are strong for long-distance, but unorganized and poor criticism may affect safety.\n\nCandidate D's problem solving and responsibility are strong, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWe need to choose one. I think Candidate C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections is highly valuable for long-distance flights, and leadership qualities are good. Concerns: unorganized and not good at criticism. Those are less severe than communication or uncooperative? Might be manageable.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message stating recommendation for Candidate C, referencing discussion (none yet) but we can say \"Considering the criteria, I think Candidate C stands out because...\" Provide evidence: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, leadership, and note concerns but weigh them.\n\nWe also need to include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
